>> title: Phở Gà
>> category: Soups
>> tags: chicken, noodles, vietnamese, soup, rice noodles
>> counters: Phở & Bánh Mì
>> aka: pho ga, phở gà, chicken pho, chicken noodle pho, Vietnamese chicken noodle soup, pho with chicken, P2
>> pairs-with: pho-bo
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 30 min
>> step.1: char over a flame 8 min
>> step.2: poach 45 min, lift the bird out
>> step.3: season, simmer 20 min, shred the meat back in
>> step.4: boil 5 min, drain into bowls
>> step.5: ladle over, finish the bowls

Char @yellow onion{1%large}(halved) and @fresh ginger{3%in}(halved lengthways) on a burner ~char{8%min} until blackened in patches, then scrape the ash away.

Poach @whole chicken{4%lb}(1.8 kg) with @&(~1)charred aromatics{}, @water{5%qt}(4.7 L), @kosher salt{1%Tbs} and @star anise{2%whole} at a bare shiver ~poach{45%min}, then lift the bird out into a bowl of cold water to stop it and set the skin. Never let the pot boil: a boil turns the broth cloudy and the breast to string.

Season @&(~1)pot{} with @fish sauce{3%Tbs}(45 mL) and @rock sugar{1/2%oz}(15 g) and ~simmer{20%min} while you pull the cooled bird apart, skin and all, and drop the meat back in. One bird is both the broth and what goes in the bowl — there is no moment at which a phở gà broth exists on its own, which is why this is one table where phở bò is two.

Boil @dried bánh phở noodles{8%oz}(225 g) in @water{4%qt}(3.8 L) ~boil{5%min} until just slippery, then drain and divide among four warmed bowls.

Ladle @&(~2)broth and chicken{} over @&(~1)noodles{} and finish with @scallions{3}(sliced), @cilantro{1/2%cup}, @yellow onion{1/4%small}(shaved paper-thin), @lime{1}(in wedges) and @bird chiles{2}(sliced).
